# rm545, the charcoal rest (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm545
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_ragnar_vance
written_by codex
title the charcoal rest
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers temper=short honesty=guarded
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk draws_the_rests_between_chapel_bells_in_charcoal
likes pickled_herring evening_line tidy_house first_snow
dislikes drizzle night_noise
fears a_silence_spoiled_by_an_extra_stroke
hopes quiet_that_will_fit_between_two_bells
topics memories +0.6 pastimes +0.5 home +0.3 weather +0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=guarded refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# draws the rests between chapel bells in charcoal, saves the longest rest for a hillside memory, and expects other hands to leave the finished count alone.

words
oath! = Smear my last rest | Ash in the bell
saying! = Count what falls quiet | Leave the hill one blank
coalrest = a blank charcoal square | a pale gap in the strokes
ashstick = a charred twig | a stub of black charcoal
hillpaper = a folded hill drawing | a soot-dark scrap
fishcurl = a curled herring strip | a piece of sharp herring
snowash = a grey snowflake | a little smudge of snow
twinebob = a cork on thread | a small tied float
cleanhem = a length of plain rag | a clean fold of cloth
cupquiet = a still cup of water | a soundless water bowl
nighttick = a faint wooden tick | a tiny roof creak
duskchar = an evening-grey smudge | a streak of late light

any
opinion @1 city mixed 1 : There are places where I can scarcely hear the thoughts inside my head. I would leave a little more quiet between roofs.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : It matters what a camp is like to live in after the account of what it produces has gone away to town.
opinion @1 road for 1 : Some roads are worth taking for the sounds that cease as you climb.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : Let me stand where one last bell can finish clearly. You may have the loud middle of the company.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : I'll remember who let me consider the goods in peace. A second speech has never made my appetite larger.
line @1 greet : Mind the blank bit. That's what I've been counting.
line @1 greet.return : I can fit your voice in again now.
line @1 farewell : Let the last sound finish of its own accord.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll remember where your part goes quiet.
line @1 ask.how : Have you had a whole stretch of quiet today?
line @1 answer.how : I'd be easier with fewer little sounds competing for my ear.
line @1 thank : You let that one end without filling the space afterwards.
line @1 decline : I won't hand over something that took all that quiet to put right.
line @1 accept_decline : I can keep your answer as short as you gave it.
line @1 sympathise : I'll stay here without adding another demand for an answer.
line @1 reassure : There may still be one clear space after all that noise.
line @1 react.news : Start with the one part you're certain of.
line @1 react.news.new : That sound hadn't entered the count till now.
line @1 react.news.known : I've a dark mark down for that one already.
line @1 react.news.doubt : A ring still hanging in the air can be mistaken for another stroke.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : I can give good news a clean place all to itself.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Lower your voice. The part that hurts doesn't need any extra ringing.
line @1 ack : Just so. Now I have the count straight.

grown
scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can fish through the evening without demanding a single interruption from a fish.
b : Does that really count as fishing? | What do you take home?
a : The hook would suggest I take the possibility seriously. It isn't the only pleasure in the arrangement. | A better knowledge of how long an ordinary stretch of water can hold my attention.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The charcoal camp taught me how many sounds are left after people stop talking.
b : What one do you hear most clearly? | Do you want to return?
a : A very small movement in cooling wood. You miss it entirely if you are waiting for a grand conclusion. | For a visit. The quiet I remember belongs partly to the age at which I heard it.

scene food_1
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Sharp herring makes me want a plain bit of bread and an interval without conversation.
b : Why the interval? | Would you eat by yourself?
a : I'm curious how long the taste will last. A rapid account of somebody's errands seldom helps me measure it. | I'd share a quiet meal willingly. Company doesn't have to be an uninterrupted performance.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A tidy room makes it possible to identify the one unfamiliar noise requiring attention.
b : Do you find it quickly? | Isn't a tidy room also rather bare?
a : If I know where the loose things ordinarily stand. A lid left askew is an extraordinarily active musician. | I keep the things I actually enjoy. There is room to see the plain spaces between.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On the first snowy morning I put the counting scrap away for one full round of bells.
b : Why that particular morning? | Can you remember the count afterwards?
a : Snow changes how the note reaches me. I'd have the pleasure of the sound before trying to preserve its measure. | Usually. I give myself one occasion on which forgetting the numbers would also be acceptable.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I choose a hill road partly for its gradual distance from town noise.
b : How far away do you go? | Do the bells reach that far?
a : Far enough to distinguish the wind going one way from my own breath going the other. | Sometimes just the last note. There is a curious comfort in hearing a familiar thing from the edge of its reach.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I trust someone who can leave a private memory on its own shelf while we talk of something else.
b : Does asking spoil the memory? | Which subject would be welcome?
a : An honest question won't. Repeated demands to display it make me more inclined to put the whole subject away. | A good piece of paper, a clean float or the change in sound before it snows.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If my temper is short, I measure out a whole bell's silence before I commit to an answer.
b : Does the question have to wait? | What if the bells are quiet?
a : If a wolf has the grace to let me think, the answer is usually worth the waiting. | I know the length of the interval. By now that little bit of the chapel can travel with me.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Good charcoal for drawing ought to leave a clear stroke without crumbling into dust straight away.
b : Do you try it before buying? | Can a broken piece still be used?
a : A modest mark on a scrap before payment seems a reasonable request, and a more useful one than asking whether it's good. | Use its broad side to darken a hillside. An accident sometimes makes a tool for another kind of stroke.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In lean times I keep the smallest bits of drawing charcoal in a folded paper packet.
b : Can they still make a whole picture? | Isn't there a better use for fuel?
a : A thumb and a clean gap can manage the important parts. A little dust is plenty for the grey round the edges. | The packet holds what falls from the stick. It wouldn't heat a spoonful of water.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I listen to a single bell until I can no longer be quite sure whether it has finished.
b : Is that a prayer for you? | How do you decide the end?
a : It serves to remind me that listening can be an act of respect even when no words are spoken. | I don't always have to decide. The small space of uncertainty is part of what I came to hear.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Drizzle on a roof will mark time in the most irregular and unhelpful fashion.
b : Do you try to count it? | Can't you enjoy it anyway?
a : The earliest drops are easy to number. They run together before I have much of a piece of music. | Sometimes I can enjoy my own annoyance with it. That is a lesser pleasure, but it passes the afternoon.

story wetchar [topic=weather]
  : I tried marking a snowy chimney on a scrap that had been rather too close to the windowsill.
  : The charcoal darkened the damp patch and ran past the outline I'd intended.
  b : Did you throw the drawing out?
  : I let it dry. The quiet shape that was left looked more like a charcoal hill in mist than anything I'd got by careful planning.

rule @rest
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let the quiet portion finish too. | A note at a distance has a different weight.

rule @night
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's a tick worth identifying before anyone rings again. | A dry roof can be an orchestra after dusk.

dlg @2 resident.hub : We can talk quietly here. My count can keep its place for a while.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : These words reached me in the gap between other sounds. #world.news#.
dlg @2 resident.bye : Leave room for the quieter half of your journey.

young
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : You may stand here if you won't rub the charcoal away.
scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I draw the silence after it rings. Look, the paper's all black except #coalrest#.
b : How did you draw nothing? | Is it a really long quiet?
a : I drew right round it. Don't put a finger there or it'll be a picture of your finger instead. | It's as long as the bit where I can imagine being up the hill with nobody calling.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm #self.trade_words#. My charcoal goes very straight for the exercises and crooked when I draw the hill.
b : What does the hill learn? | Do your exercises get smoky?
a : Nothing. It's already a fine hill before I begin putting sums on the other side. | Only if I fold them inwards. I've learnt to keep a decent calculation out of my mountains now.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A piece of herring curls into quite a neat little bell if you put the tail end upwards.
b : Can you ring it? | Can you eat your bell?
a : Once. It makes a little slap on the plate and after that it's only fish again. | That's how you get it to keep quiet for a really long time.

scene family_1
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show this drawing to #self.mother# before the bells make me change it.
b : Can you put another drawing on top? | What part do you want to show first?
a : I'd slip a clean sheet between the pictures. Charcoal tries to put itself on both sides. | The bit left bare for the hill. It wasn't nearly so noisy where the charcoal used to burn.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first snow makes everything outside look like my untouched bit of paper.
b : Will you draw the snow? | Won't the bell still ring?
a : I'd have to put charcoal all round the whole street. I might draw just one snowy chimney instead. | Yes. But its edges seem to go soft when all the roofs are wearing white.

scene home_1
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My drawings have one shelf to themselves with nothing loose that can go walking over the hills.
b : Can a thing walk on paper? | What's allowed on the shelf?
a : A button can roll. You should see the road one little button made across a whole quiet valley. | Drawings and the clean cloth that goes between. The charcoal has to sleep well away from the clean edges.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A moth on a bell drawing looks surprisingly like a missing piece of the hill.
b : Did you put it there? | How could you tell it was a moth?
a : No. It arrived without asking, the way little moving things so often do. | It took the hillside off in two pieces and flew away with both of them.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Up at the charcoal camp even the smoke seemed in no hurry to go anywhere.
b : Was everything black? | Would you sleep back there?
a : No. The hill had green on it and there was quite a lot of sky left even after a busy morning. | I want an unbroken stretch of night where the roof doesn't count out the town for me.

scene day_1
when topic=day self.dislikes=night_noise
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Once the chapel bell finishes at night there's a little bit of quiet a louder sound keeps barging into.
b : Why don't you like that? | What larger sound?
a : It's the cart or a door just when I'm listening for the nice quiet part. It muddles up my whole page. | Any one that could have waited till morning in my considered opinion.

story crookedvalley [topic=memories]
  : I folded my hill drawing to keep it in a pocket and forgot to slip a clean sheet inside.
  : When I opened it the next morning there were hills on either valley wall.
  b : Did you draw another camp?
  : The second was a reflection. I left a big patch of untouched valley so the two could have some quiet between them.

rule @mark
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One black mark and a properly long rest. | The square without charcoal is the one I meant.

rule @snow
when concept=bark self.likes=first_snow
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Snow's rubbed some quiet onto all the roofs. | Fewer black strokes for the chimney tops today.

dlg @1 resident.hub : You can see the drawing provided your fingers keep clear of the edges.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=child] : I'm #self.trade_words#. I keep a good clean bit for the figures and do the hill on the reverse.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Don't take a black thumbprint away with you.
graft resident.hub
choice Why did you leave a white square on your hill? -> coal_gap
node coal_gap
say That's the quiet between the chapel's last loud ring and the rest of town starting up. It's the best bit. I did it by leaving it alone.
choice Can I look more closely? -> coal_near
choice I'll keep my hands here. -> hub
node coal_near
say Look with your eyes. All the charcoal on the rest of the page is trying terribly hard to get inside that square.
choice I'll keep my hands here. -> hub


adolescent
scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll let a friend add a charcoal mark provided we have agreed which sounds are worth counting.
b : What isn't worth a mark? | Do you let a friend choose?
a : The second echo pretending to be a bell all by itself. We'd end up arguing with our own room. | For a separate row, certainly. Two counts can disagree without one being deliberately spoilt.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=evening_line
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A float has its own rests. Sometimes it stays motionless enough to disappear into the water behind it.
b : What shows where the float is? | Is quiet good for fishing?
a : The thread holds a faint sweep of evening light. That gives my eyes somewhere to return. | It's good for me. I wouldn't presume to answer for a fish before it decides to enquire.

story oddstroke [topic=pastimes]
  : I wrote what I thought was an extra bell on a scrap and carried it outside to count again.
  : The extra stroke returned at precisely the same interval.
  b : Was the chapel ringing an extra one?
  : My little cork float was knocking the side of its bowl on my sill. I moved it and gave the chapel back its usual count.
